sections.text:
The third BattlePass season, “Morbus Imperium”, has started in EFT: Arena, featuring new rewards:
- FN P90 (Scourge) submachine gun with a unique setup;
- New weapon mods and paint kits;
- New tactical clothing;
- New gear: helmets, body armor, chest rigs, and plate carriers;
- Blue Force Gear PLATEminus V2 plate carriers in various configurations;
- Unique MSA Millennium Riot Control gas mask;
- New “Morbus” and “Panacea” Ref Crates.

BattlePass rewards are unlocked as you level up and purchased with Battle Points, a seasonal currency unique to each season.

Unused Battle Points from the previous season were automatically converted into “Echo Belli” crates at a 1:30 ratio. Players receive an additional crate for any remaining balance over 15 Battle Points. 14 or fewer Battle Points are lost.

Battle Pass levels can be purchased on the EFT: Arena and Escape from Tarkov websites, as well as in the Epic Games Store.

A new Tactical Map “The Lab” has been added, featuring more than 50 points of interest, three floor levels, and unique rewards:
- Tactical clothing;
- Weapon paint kits;
- New helmet covers;
- Gear, including new variations of Blue Force Gear PLATEminus V2 plate carriers;
- “Morbus” and “Panacea” crates;
- Battle Points for the third BattlePass season.
Rewards are unlocked using Tactical Tokens, which players earn for certain actions in combat. Tokens are only valid on their corresponding map. You can select the desired map on the BattlePass screen using the button in the upper-right corner.

The Lab Tactical Map also features currency exchange points where you can exchange currency for crates from the new season and Tactical Tokens.

The Lab Tactical Map can be purchased on the EFT: Arena and Escape from Tarkov websites, as well as in the Epic Games Store.

- Added separate sound effects for eliminating an opponent with a body shot or a headshot;
- Reworked the sound effects played when taking damage;
- Increased the volume of hit sounds on the character.

- Added a red indicator around the edges of the screen showing the direction of incoming fire;
- Improved the visual feedback when the character is hit.

The effects have been tuned to make hits more noticeable without overwhelming the screen during combat.

- Upper spawn was strengthened;
- Positions that allowed players to attack opponents directly at spawn have been closed off;
- Added a new route to mid;
- Removed the ability to shoot through the spawn from the stairs at Point A;
- Mine zones were reworked.

- Interior layout was reworked and the number of hard-to-check corners were reduced;
- Cover shape and placement at the objectives have been changed;
- Added a new route from the street for the team starting the round near the cable car;
- Cover throughout the location was reworked.

Win a match on the following locations:
- Win a match on Fort;
- Win a match on Equator;
- Win a match on Bowl;
- Win a match on Chop Shop;
- Win a match on Bay 5.

PMC and weapon progression XP gained in the following modes has been increased:
- BlastGang by 35%;
- TeamFight by 30%;
- ShootOut by 20%;

- Adjusted the VoIP and radio volume;
- Adjusted the volume of interference sounds in Spectator mode;
- Balanced the ambient sounds on EMERCOM, Dorms, and Equator;
- Adjusted the equipment, jumping, landing, and body/weapon drop sounds;
- Adjusted the sound of transitioning to prone from a sprint;
- Balanced the volume of the match readiness screen;
- Improved the sound occlusion on Fort;
- Increased the range of the bomb signal in BlastGang mode;
- Enhanced the stereo effect of gunshots fired in close proximity to the player;
- Updated the post-match screen audio: balanced the volume of existing sounds and added new ones;
- Fixed the speakers on Skybridge in the large hall near the spawn point;
- Fixed an issue where sound volume between rounds could change even when interface sounds were disabled;
- Added a system for mixing first-person gunshot sounds when indoors, in open areas, and near openings.

- Improved the hit registration system for weapon shots;
- Reduced the time it takes the server to process player deaths;
- Fixed an issue that could cause multiple players to crash out of a match.

- Fixed an issue where a second confirmation window appeared when attempting to decline quick reconnection;
- Fixed the incorrect display of received rewards in Match History;
- Fixed issues with various effects interacting with smoke grenades;
- Fixed potential causes of enemies becoming invisible;
- Several other minor fixes.

- Added an in-game community survey system;
- Fixed an issue where the hotkey UI wasn't updated after replenishing ammo at a Supply Crate;
- Fixed an issue where gates failed to open after the start of a round;
- Improved the perception of shot sounds coming from behind the player.

A post-match rewards system has been added to the game. After the match ends, the player can get the participation reward on the "Team" screen.

Every match played grants experience. The amount of experience depends on several conditions:

- Match outcome (win, defeat, place claimed);
- Obtaining MVP;
- Activity during the match (kills, assists, points captured and other actions);
- First win of the day bonus.

After accumulating a certain amount of experience, the player gets a reward. The information about the reward is shown on the Team screen and in the main menu.

At first the reward will be in the form of an Echo Belli crate. In future the list of rewards will be expanded.

The cost of the VSK-94 and 9A-91 has been adjusted following the previous balance patch that reduced Assault weapon costs.
- Reduced the VSK-94 Meta Score to 800;
- educed the 9A-91 Meta Score to 800.

Red:
- Changed both ballistic plates to SAPI III+;
- Changed the scope to OKP-7;
- Replaced the MAWL-C1+ with NcStar TBL.

Jaeger:
- Changed both ballistic plates to SAPI III+;
- Changed the helmet to AirFrame OD.

Leon:
- Changed both ballistic plates to SAPI III+;
- Changed the helmet to STRIKE;
- Changed the headset to ComTac VI.

Alpha:
- Added one more box magazine with PP ammo;
- Changed the body armor to 6B13.

Concrete:
- Changed the body armor to Gladiator-S with Cult Locust and SAPI III+ plates;
- Added one more box magazine;
- Added the AN/PEQ-15 to the weapon.

Voron:
- Added side plates;
- Added Pilad TargetRing reflex sight;
- Added the MAWL-C1+ to the weapon.

Stinger:
- Changed the ballistic plates to ESAPI IV;
- Changed the helmet to the USEC hat;
- Added Crossbow glasses;
- Changed the headset to MSA Sordin.

Python:
- Changed the ballistic plates to ESAPI IV;
- Changed the helmet to Domontovich hat;
- Changed the headset to ProFlex DX5;
- Removed the suppressor from the weapon.

Foch:
- Changed the ballistic plates to ESAPI IV;
- Changed the headset to ProFlex DX5;
- Changed the helmet to Cowboy hat;
- Changed the buttstock to GL-SHOCK;
- Added the MAWL-C1+ to the weapon;
- Changed the handguard to Magpul MOE;
- Changed the front grip to DD Enhanced M-LOK.

Dagger:
- Changed the helmet to FLUX;
- Changed the headset to ComTac V.

Spoke:
- Changed the headset to Liberator;
- Changed the headwear to ULACH;
- Added the 6B34 goggles.

Carbon:
- Changed the front grip to SE-5;
- Changed the armor to A18 Skanda;
- Added one more magazine.

- Fixed the compatibility issues of FLUX, Caiman and NeoSteel helmets with ballistic goggles;
- Added TEP-300 and ProFlex DX5 earplugs to all classes;
- Fixed the Meta Score cost of the GL-CORE S buttstock. Previously 300, now 763 to match similar stocks;
- Fixed the Meta Score cost of the M32 (White) headset. Previously 277, now 250 to match the standard version;
- Fixed the localization of the SR-3M W-Task: Eliminate 2+ enemies with headshots within 5 seconds in any game mode;
- Fixed an issue where BEAR Lonsdale pants were available to USEC instead of BEAR;
- Fixed an issue where achievements for the new task chain were not granted. Missing achievements have now been automatically awarded.

- ComTac, GSSh-01, Razor Digital, and Razor Slim headsets can now be worn with Crye AirFrame Ears and Chops;
- Removed the P22 stimulant injector from the Armory;
- Added original icons to the First Blood, The Time to Live and the Time to Die, and Legend of the Arena achievements;
- Changed the condition of the Factory Tactical Map ShootOut token from “Claim at least 6th place” to “Claim at least 5th place”.

- For Last Hero, CheckPoint, and ShootOut, the logic that invalidated a match when one or more players disconnected and failed to return in time has been disabled;
- For ShootOut:
  - Doubled the kill experience;
  - Doubled the weapon progression leveling experience;
  - Reduced the match placement experience.

Weapons (Meta score reduction)
- AS VAL — −210;
- AS VAL — −210;
- MCX — −210;
- HK 416A5 — −200;
- Radian Model 1 — −190;
- NL545 (GP) — −200;
- M4A1 — −200;
- NL545 (DI) — −190;
- M16A1 — −130;
- Mk 12 SPR — −180.

Following mixed feedback regarding overall Meta score limits, we are slightly reducing the Meta score cost of support gear and stimulants in presets.

These changes collectively free up approximately 100–250 Meta score points across all classes, primarily improving Assault build flexibility.

- Stimulants Meta score reduced by 10–30;
- Magazines Meta score reduced by 10–150;
- Headsets Meta score reduced by 20–50.

Slight improvements have been made to core Scout ammunition performance.

These changes are intended to improve consistency when penetrating class 4 armor and slightly increase headshot effectiveness, while still not guaranteeing outcomes.

- 4.6×30mm FMJ SX — damage increased from 45 to 46;
- 5.7×28mm SS190 — penetration increased from 37 to 38;
- .45 ACP AP — penetration increased from 36 to 37;
- 9×19mm PBP gzh — damage increased to 51; penetration increased to 40;
- 9×21mm 7N42 “Zubilo” — damage increased to 53; penetration increased to 39.

In older patches, due to the inherent weakness of the Enforcer class, bolt-action ammunition retained a performance gap that resulted in ~10% chance to fail penetrating class 5 armor plates. This gap has now been removed to reduce Enforcer dominance and ensure consistent chest-shot lethality with bolt-action rifles using the ammo types listed below.
- 7.62×51mm Ball 11 Long Range — penetration increased from 59 to 63;
- 7.62×54R Tungsten Carbide AP — penetration increased from 61 to 66.

- Removed third progression tier for VSK-94 and 9A-91 (duplicate module was available by default);
- Adjusted unlock requirements for Steyr AUG A3 5.56×45 — now requires Ref Loyalty Level 2;
- Fixed NL545 camo painting issues;
- Fixed issue allowing two headset items to be equipped simultaneously (BattlePass S2);
- Fixed incompatibility between Hera Arms CQR and GL-Core S stocks;
- Fixed compatibility issue between certain headsets and AirFrame Chops;
- Fixed clipping on Galvion Caiman Hybrid helmet;
- Fixed W-Task localization for SR-3M;
- Rash guard “Arena Warrior” is granted to players who did not receive it previously.

- The ‘Arena Gladiator’ rash guard from the Tactical Map has been replaced with the correct version in the BattlePass — the ‘Arena Warrior’ rash guard;
- Fixed the duplication of rewards on the Tactical Map screen when switching between the Customs Tactical Map and the Factory Tactical Map;
- Fixed the absence of the “Tagilla (RU)” announcer voice in the voice selection menu;
- Fixed the display of Tactical Map availability after purchase before re-entering the game client;
- Fixed the absence of team armbands on the FORT Gladiator-S plate carrier in the ShootOut mode widget before the start of a round;
- Fixed the display of durability for melee weapons;
- Fixed the display of the Match MVP icon in the Match History;
- Fixed the display of the ComTac VI (Black) and ComTac VI (Ranger Green) headset icons;
- Fixed the incorrect calculation of player statistics following the 0.5.0 update;
- Added the display of minutes to the time format shown in the statistics table for matches in ShootOut mode;
- The TEP-300 and CENS earplugs are now permitted for use with the Titan Aramid (Rudiarius) helmet;
- Fixed the localization in the ShootOut clash widget;
- The ULACH helmet (Black) is no longer available to the Scout class;
- Fixed the MP of the M32 headset (White), now matching the original M32;
- Corrected the stats for the IRBIS 30AL grip (0/12 as in EFT instead of 0.5/10);
- Added a second progression tier for the Radian Model 1, with the reward being the A-TACS AU camouflage;
- Corrected the incorrect unlock condition for the M/98 (Gold) camouflage;
- Fixed the price of the BGV-QDK tactical grip (90,000 roubles instead of 90,000 GP);
- The A.R.M.S. scope mount is now only available to the Marksman class, rather than all classes;
- Fixed the sensitivity changes when using SRO reflex sights;
- Fixed the localization of the built-in armor in the Gladiator-S (Death is Inevitable) plate carrier, as well as the related preset bug;
- CQCM mask (Black) is now available to all classes;
- Added the missing progression tiers for the NL545 with the missing locked attachments;
- Added a missing tier to the PKP progression with the missing locked attachment;
- The cost of the Radian Model 1 base weapon has been raised to match the M4A1 price;
- Added the compatibility between the Ushanka hat and GSSh-01 headset, as in Escape from Tarkov.

A new BattlePass season “Casus Belli” is now live in EFT: Arena, featuring over 70 unique rewards, including:
- Saiga-12K full-auto shotgun with a unique skin “Redline”;
- New reflex sights and weapon attachments;
- New tactical clothing and weapon camouflages;
- Full gear sets: helmets, body armor, chest rigs, and plate carriers, including the new FORT Gladiator-S plate carrier in multiple variants;
- Lega Medals and “Echo Belli” crates for EFT: Arena.
- BattlePass rewards unlock through progression and are purchased with Battle Points, a seasonal currency unique to each season.

All Battle Points from Season 1 have been automatically converted into “Ref’s Drop I” crates at a 1:40 rate. Any remainder above 20 Battle Points is converted into 1 “Ref’s Drop I” crate, 19 or fewer are forfeited.

BattlePass “Casus Belli” levels can be purchased via the EFT: Arena and Escape from Tarkov websites.

Added a new Tactical Map “Factory” featuring over 40 points of interest and unique rewards:
- Voiceover by guest announcer Tagilla (RU / EN);
- Unique tactical clothing;
- Weapon camouflages;
- New masks and eyewear;
- Gear (helmets, body armor, chest rigs, and plate carriers), including the FORT Gladiator-S plate carrier in multiple variants;
- “Echo Belli” crates for EFT: Arena;
- Battle Points for BattlePass Season 2;
- Rewards are unlocked using Tactical Tokens earned through specific in-match actions. Tokens are map-specific — Factory tokens cannot be used for Customs and vice versa.

The Factory Tactical Map can be purchased via both the EFT: Arena and Escape from Tarkov websites.

- Added the ability to select and purchase Tactical Maps from previous seasons;
- Tactical Map progress is now permanently saved regardless of profile resets or Prestige;
- Rewards from all Tactical Maps, such as BattlePass experience and Battle Points, are now applied to the current active BattlePass;
- Tactical Tokens are gained only for the Tactical Map selected by the player.

- “Ref’s Drop I” crate is no longer available for purchase with Battle Points;
- Unused crates remain in the player’s inventory;
- A limited number can still be obtained via the Customs Tactical Map.

- All rounds now run in parallel, spectator stands have been removed, significantly reducing downtime between fights;
- Added the ability to switch presets after each fight;
- All team colors have been removed except Red for enemies and Blue for allies;
- For easier identification in the leaderboard, unique team icons in the form of animals have been added;
- The mode’s user interface has been fully redesigned;
- ShootOut is now available on the following locations: Air Pit, Block, Equator, and Factory.

The race for unique number-tagged guns has already begun. Be among the first thousand players to complete the new W-Tasks and receive a personalized weapon number tag!

Weapons that received new W-Tasks and paint options:
- FN P90;
- AS VAL;
- SR-3M;
- Saiga-12K;
- Saiga-12K FA;
- Saiga-12K FA “Redline”.

Weapon Tasks have been added for all listed weapons and become available after full leveling progression.

- Each task line completion grants a unique achievement;
- Some tasks can be completed in parallel;
- Completion unlocks Armory rewards: weapons, armor, gear, masks, medical items, and unique camo sets.

- Added achievements for the new task line;
- Added achievements for ShootOut and Last Hero modes;
- Added an achievement for completing BattlePass Season 2 «Casus Belli».

- Colt M16A1;
- Colt M16A2 (in the Mk12 Mod 0 marksman rifle preset variant);
- CGNL NL545 (DI);
- CGNL NL545 (GP);
- AK-308;
- AS VAL MOD.4;
- Marlin MXLR;
- KAC SR-25 (Taupe) (in M110 preset variants);
- TheAKGuy AK-50;
- TKPD carbine.

The SWORD International Mk-18 marksman rifle, previously only available in Escape from Tarkov, has also been added to the EFT: Arena Armory.

- 6B45 body armor:
- 6B45 armored rig (Medic);
- 6B45 armored rig (General Purpose);
- 6B45 armored rig (Assault);
- Crye Precision JPC plate carrier;
- Tac-Kek JayPC plate carrier (Black);
- Tac-Kek JayPC plate carrier (OD Green).

Due to limited modification capabilities, availability of alternatives, and balancing complexity of real prototypes, the following weapons have been removed from the Armory:
- Molot VPO-136 Vepr-KM;
- Molot ADAR 2-15;
- SAG AK-545 Short;
- FN SCAR-L FDE;
- FN SCAR-H;
- Steyr AUG A1;
- Steyr AUG A3;
- Kalashnikov PKM;
- U.S. Ordnance M60E4;
- U.S. Ordnance M60E6;
- Makarov PM;
- Tokarev TT-33 (Golden);
- Glock 19X;
- Chiappa Rhino 200DS;
- MTs-255-12;
- HK MP5K;
- Soyuz-TM STM-9;
- IWI UZI;
- IWI UZI PRO SMG;
- Mosin rifle (Infantry);
- Kalashnikov AKS-74N;
- TOZ Simonov SKS.

Most of the attachments from removed duplicates were transferred to the progression trees of similar appropriate weapons.

We continue to follow the same principle as before — the longer the barrel, the greater the recoil reduction bonus and the higher the ergonomics penalty. Based on this, the following changes were made:
- Barrel parameters have been standardized for better clarity and more meaningful choice.
- Handguards no longer reduce recoil but instead compensate for the ergonomics penalty from barrels.

Base stats of some weapons have been adjusted to fine-tune recoil and ergonomics. This affected the following:
- All AK, AKM, and AK-100 series weapons;
- Steyr AUG A1;
- Steyr AUG A3;
- HK G36;
- HK 416A5;
- FN SCAR-L;
- FN SCAR-H;
- SIG MCX-SPEAR;
- SIG MCX .300;
- CMMG Mk47 Mutant;
- Rifle Dynamics RD-704;
- Aklys Defense Velociraptor;
- All machine guns;
- All bolt-action and marksman rifles in 7.62x51, 7.62x54R, and .338 calibers

- The stat spread of pistol grips, foregrips, and stocks has been reduced;
- All grip and stock stats have been significantly updated.

We hope these changes will allow players to build weapons based not only on stats but also on aesthetic preferences, without dividing mods into “bad” and “good”.

Customization items from Escape from Tarkov have been added to EFT: Arena:
- USEC voice “Rob” — Prestige 3;
- BEAR voice “Vitaly” — Prestige 3;;
- USEC voice “Nikita” — available via Twitch Drops or website purchase;
- BEAR voice “Nikita” — available via Twitch Drops or website purchase;
- USEC head “Shawn” — Prestige 5;
- BEAR head “Basilevs” — Prestige 5;
- Gesture “OK” — Prestige 2;
- Gestures “Rock”, “Scissors”, “Paper” — Prestige 1;

- Added a new option — Match History, allowing players to view detailed statistics of their matches:
  - Match history is available in the “HISTORY” tab on the Career screen;
  - Matches played within the last six months are saved into match history;
  - 12 most recent matches are loaded at a time, with scroll support.
- In Match History, players can view general statistics:
  - game mode;
  - map;
  - date;
  - match result;
  - K/D of match participants;
  - Match MVP.
- In addition to general information, Match History displays match details:
  - experience gained;
  - money earned;
  - headshot percentage;
  - accuracy;
  - devices planted and deactivated in BlastGang mode;
  - objectives captured in CheckPoint mode.
- Match History does not display invalid or custom matches.

- Added a new option — View Profile, allowing players to view information about other players.
- To view your own or another player’s profile, right-click the player’s nickname and select “View Profile”:
  - A player's profile can be viewed in:
    - premade group;
    - group invite window;
    - chat window;
    - friends list;
    - Match History.
  - A profile cannot be viewed during an ongoing match.
- The “View Profile” screen displays a brief player statistical overview similar to EFT but adapted to EFT: Arena specifics.
- Below the player statistics panel, there is a Rare Achievements panel.

- PPSh-41 received 1 additional progression level:
  - Level 2 unlocks the drum magazine;
  - Level 3 unlocks the Golden TT.
- Atomic Defense CQCM (Black) ballistic mask is now available to all classes.
- All CQCM mask variants are now fully identical in stats to the Atomic Defense CQCM (Black).
- All variants of the DevTac Samurai Menpo Mask and the Work Peak training mask can now be worn together with helmets:
  - Exceptions that prevent mask usage: Tank Crew helmet, Champion helmet, and when using certain face protection attachments on helmets.

Changes to the in-game task line "To Great Heights!"
- You can now accept and complete tasks from this task line in both EFT: Arena and EFT;
- Rouble transfer for the task "To Great Heights! - Part 4" is now available in both EFT: Arena and in EFT;
- Adjusted the task rewards and their objectives;
- Added new tasks to the task line.

For players who had not completed "To Great Heights!" prior to the update, progress on active tasks has been reset and appropriate compensation has been issued

- Fixed an issue where match results would occasionally not appear after completion in certain modes;
- Fixed an issue where using medical items and the Resupply Crate at the same time could cause the weapon to not reappear in the player’s hands after reusing medical items;
- Fixed the player mute resetting at the start of a new match;
- Fixed the incompatibility between the Champion helmet and M32 headset;
- Fixed the incorrect display of in-game currency balance after making purchases in the Armory;
- Fixed an issue causing the Announcer’s voice lines to cut off at the beginning of a match;
- Other fixes.

- Disabled the Escape from Tarkov locations which were available during the in-game event “Dubak”: Dorms, Base, and EMERCOM;
- Disabled the snow and New Year decorations on Fort, Bay 5, and Block.

These changes will not affect the BattlePass or the Customs Tactical Map. The 20 additional BattlePass levels and the New Year tree checkpoint will remain available until the end of Season 1.

Simplified the W-Task conditions. The number of required sub-tasks remains unchanged.

- ASh-12:
  - Eliminate enemies;
  - Eliminate 30+ enemies within one match;
  - Win a clutch against 2+ enemies in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- AK-12:
  - Eliminate 3+ enemies within one magazine;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies with headshots in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- SR-25:
  - Eliminate 6 enemies with headshots within one life (new rounds don’t reset the counter);
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies with headshots within one round in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- Mk47 Mutant:
  - Eliminate 4 enemies with headshots in a row;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies without dying in the round in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- MCX:
  - Eliminate 30 enemies within one match;
  - Eliminate 4 enemies within one life (new rounds don’t reset the counter).
- M4A1:
  - Eliminate 3+ enemies with headshots within 12 seconds;
  - Eliminate 4 enemies with headshots within one life (new rounds don’t reset the counter).
- MDR 5.56:
  - Eliminate 3+ enemies within 15 seconds;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies with headshots within one round in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- MDR 7.62:
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies with headshots within one magazine.
- MP7A1:
  - Eliminate enemies;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies within one magazine;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies within one round in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- KRISS Vector 9×19:
  - Eliminate 3+ enemies within one life (new rounds don’t reset the counter);
  - Eliminate 3+ enemies within 12 seconds;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies within one round in BlastGang or TeamFight mode.
- KRISS Vector .45 ACP:
  - Eliminate enemies;
  - Eliminate 2+ enemies within 10 seconds.

- Increased the experience gain by up to 40% across all game modes.
  - For wins, draws, and losses;
  - For kills, headshot kills, double kills, and kill streaks;
  - For successful device activation and deactivation in BlastGang mode.

Rebalanced the damage calculation parameters to stabilize ammo behavior and eliminate the armor "bullet sponge" effect.

- Increased the blunt damage for all ammo types;
- Reduced the built-in armor of class 3 armor vests and armored rigs to class 2;
- Adjusted the blunt damage reduction parameters for all armor types.

Increased the meta score for most ammo types;
- Reduced the meta score for class 4 and 3 plates;
- Reduced the meta score for all helmets and masks;
- Reduced the meta score for all weapons;
- Increased the armor penetration value of 7.62x54R Tungsten Carbide AP to 62;
- Reduced the overheat buildup speed by 30% for weapons using 9x39 ammo, including:
  - 9A-91;
  - VSK-94;
  - SR-3M;
  - AS VAL;
  - VSS Vintorez.

- Assault now has access to all armor vests and armored rigs that don't protect the neck area;
- Enforcer now has access to all armor vests and armored rigs that apply minimal mobility penalties;
- Scout now has access to all armor vests and armored rigs that don't protect the groin and/or stomach area;
- Marksman now has access to all armor vests and armored rigs without additional armor elements;
- Updated the base presets to reflect the balance changes.

- Initial configuration of Peltor TEP-300 tactical ear plug has been completed to create a unique sound profile. Future updates will also include an additional tweaking to take into account the equipment being worn;
- Removed the delay and additional jump force restrictions that were introduced in Patch 0․3․4․1;
- Reduced the penalty that limited leaning speed while moving;

Fixed multiple character control issues caused by the movement system changes introduced in Patch 0.3.4:
- Fixed an issue where the character could not start sprinting after sharp-turning by more than 90 degrees;
- Fixed an issue where sprinting was interrupted upon landing after a jump - now, the character will continue sprinting if they were sprinting before jumping;
- Fixed several issues where the character would not respond to input when using Continuous mode for aiming, movement, or sprinting;
- Fixed an issue where the character exited aiming mode when turning and pressing the sprint key while using Continuous mode;
- Fixed an issue with key press priority between sprinting and aiming modes in various situations.

Added BattlePass: Season 1:
- As part of the BattlePass, all rewards are available to players for free;
- The BattlePass includes over 70 rewards: new weapon Radian Model 1, reflex sights, unique earplugs, helmets, tactical clothing, weapon paint kits, masks, vests and plate carriers, Lega Medals, new "Ref's Drop" crates for EFT: Arena;
- Rewards are unlocked as you progress through the BattlePass and are purchased using the currency — Battle Points;
  - Please note that the currency is unique to each season.

We’ve considered player feedback and adjusted the approach to content creation and certain BattlePass mechanics.

Changes include:

- Removed the EFT loot crates from BP rewards;
- Added an exchange of Battle Points for the new crate "Ref's Drop" for players who accumulate a large number of Battle Points:
  - The crate cannot be transferred to EFT.
- Adjusted the selection and quantity of rewards based on player feedback after the end of BattlePass Season 0;
- Added numerous functionable rewards: weapons, attachments, helmets, headsets, vests and plate carriers;
- New tactical clothing with unique gloves and appearance:
  - More attention was given to elements visible to players in combat (gloves and sleeves) when designing the tactical clothing.

Added the new Tactical Map:
- An interactive map of Customs featuring points of interest;
- Contains over 30 points of interest with rewards such as:
  - Announcer voiceover by Nikita Buyanov (RU);
  - New tactical clothing, including unique Hawaii shirts;
  - Weapon camouflages;
  - New facewear and eyewear;
  - Equipment (helmets, vests, chest rigs, and plate carriers);
  - “Ref’s Drop” crates for EFT: Arena;
  - Battle Points for BattlePass Season 1.
- Unlocking a reward requires spending one or more Tactical Tokens;
- Tokens are earned in-match by eliminating opponents with various weapon types and winning in different modes;
